WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.402 --> 00:00:03.570
-The House voted
to impeach President Trump

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:04.904
for inciting last week's
Capitol insurrection,

00:00:04.904 --> 00:00:07.339
making him the first
and only president in history

00:00:07.339 --> 00:00:08.708
to be impeached twice.

00:00:08.708 --> 00:00:11.811
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:11.811 --> 00:00:15.214
♪♪

00:00:15.214 --> 00:00:17.049
Today was historic
in many ways,

00:00:17.049 --> 00:00:19.018
not the least of which was
the President

00:00:19.018 --> 00:00:20.586
became the first in history

00:00:20.586 --> 00:00:22.188
to be impeached
for a second time.

00:00:22.188 --> 00:00:23.690
As far as anyone can tell,

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:26.292
he has no discernible defense,
no legal strategy,

00:00:26.292 --> 00:00:29.595
and very few allies left
outside of the House GOP.

00:00:29.595 --> 00:00:31.897
Several of his lawyers from the
last impeachment have bailed,

00:00:31.897 --> 00:00:33.633
his former home, New York City,

00:00:33.633 --> 00:00:35.368
revoked all its contracts
with him,

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:37.570
his banks and major donors
are all fleeing.

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:39.438
Even Mitch McConnell
has signaled

00:00:39.438 --> 00:00:41.508
that he might be willing
to turn on Trump.

00:00:41.508 --> 00:00:42.842 line:0%
-According to
"The New York Times,"

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:45.578 line:0%
Senator Mitch McConnell
is pleased

00:00:45.578 --> 00:00:48.347 line:0%
that Democrats are moving
to impeach the President.

00:00:48.347 --> 00:00:50.516 line:0%
"The Times" reporting
that McConnell believes

00:00:50.516 --> 00:00:53.819 line:0%
the move will make it easier
to purge President Trump

00:00:53.819 --> 00:00:55.355 line:0%
from the Republican Party.

00:00:55.355 --> 00:00:59.659 line:0%
-Axios is reporting that there's
a better than 50-50 chance

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:01.694 line:0%
that Senate Majority Leader
Mitch McConnell

00:01:01.694 --> 00:01:04.630 line:0%
would vote
to convict President Trump

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:06.633 line:0%
in an impeachment trial.

00:01:06.633 --> 00:01:08.801
-That's significant,
because if you watch movies,

00:01:08.801 --> 00:01:11.270
you know "pleased" is
the highest level of happiness

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:12.738
for villains.

00:01:12.738 --> 00:01:15.808
"The emperor is most pleased
with your efforts, Lord Vader."

00:01:15.808 --> 00:01:17.276
Of course McConnell is pleased.

00:01:17.276 --> 00:01:18.777
He's like a guy
who robbed a bank,

00:01:18.777 --> 00:01:21.347
jumped on a helicopter to Fiji,
and pulled up the rope ladder,

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:23.215
leaving his accomplice
stranded on the roof

00:01:23.215 --> 00:01:24.583
as the cops close in.

00:01:24.583 --> 00:01:26.352
"Mitch, Mitch, come back."

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:30.122
"Uh, sorry, Donald. I can't
hear you over the rotors."

00:01:30.122 --> 00:01:35.261
[ Laughing as Mitch McConnell ]

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:37.563
Even Trump's most precious
friends in the world,

00:01:37.563 --> 00:01:40.232
his closest allies,
his wingmen and therapists,

00:01:40.232 --> 00:01:42.702
the Fox &amp; Friends are torn

00:01:42.702 --> 00:01:45.205
about whether to stick
with Trump or bail on him.

00:01:45.205 --> 00:01:48.307
-Why fracture unnecessarily?

00:01:48.307 --> 00:01:50.810
-Because, Brian,
you're talking about

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:53.112
people who work in the Congress,

00:01:53.112 --> 00:01:56.482
and we're talking about
the Congress was under attack
last week.

00:01:56.482 --> 00:01:58.717
It was looted. There was a riot.

00:01:58.717 --> 00:02:02.522
-So is Portland every day,
and nobody cared on the left.

00:02:02.522 --> 00:02:04.456
-Brian --
-Those people have lives, too.

00:02:04.456 --> 00:02:06.058
Just because they don't
have medallions

00:02:06.058 --> 00:02:07.927
to go through metal detectors
every day.

00:02:07.927 --> 00:02:09.862
All the state houses
and the police houses

00:02:09.862 --> 00:02:12.465
that were ransacked,
and nobody cared?

00:02:12.465 --> 00:02:14.667
-I don't think what
they were doing in Portland

00:02:14.667 --> 00:02:17.303
was trying
to overthrow democracy.
-Police stations?

00:02:17.303 --> 00:02:18.972
-Let's put the shoe
on the other foot.

00:02:18.972 --> 00:02:21.441
If a Democratic president --

00:02:21.441 --> 00:02:25.277
a Democrat president
did what happened last week,

00:02:25.277 --> 00:02:26.946
a week ago today,

00:02:26.946 --> 00:02:29.348
would the Republicans
in the House and the Senate

00:02:29.348 --> 00:02:31.751
move to impeach him
if they could?

00:02:31.751 --> 00:02:33.552
The answer is yes.

00:02:33.552 --> 00:02:35.955
-Guys, guys,
you're both terrible.

00:02:35.955 --> 00:02:38.958
Man, I'd say that was the worst
thing to happen to a group
of friends this week,

00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:40.460
except they announced
they were making

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:42.962
a "Sex and the City" reboot
without Samantha.

00:02:42.962 --> 00:02:44.197
How's that even going to work?

00:02:44.197 --> 00:02:45.431
Three women in a coffee shop

00:02:45.431 --> 00:02:46.999
talking thoughtfully
about their lives

00:02:46.999 --> 00:02:49.235
and then just a big old
dead spot

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:51.070
where there should be
a delightfully hacky

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:52.872
double entendre about sex.

00:02:52.872 --> 00:02:55.975
"Harry says it's a turnoff
that I'm so anal retentive."

00:02:58.444 --> 00:03:00.379
Oh, right, she's not here.

00:03:00.379 --> 00:03:01.947
But you know
you've sunk to a new low

00:03:01.947 --> 00:03:04.784
when you're a Republican getting
reprimanded by Steve Doocy.

00:03:04.784 --> 00:03:05.985
Do you think
if we just let Trump

00:03:05.985 --> 00:03:07.653
fly off to Mar-a-Lago next week

00:03:07.653 --> 00:03:09.355
without consequences,
that'll be that

00:03:09.355 --> 00:03:10.723
and everyone will just move on?

00:03:10.723 --> 00:03:13.860
He incited a violent mob
to attack the Capitol.

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:16.863
I can't even put a new
welcome mat in front of my door

00:03:16.863 --> 00:03:18.931
without getting reprimanded
from my co-op board.

00:03:18.931 --> 00:03:21.968
So with a handful of his closest
allies abandoning him

00:03:21.968 --> 00:03:25.404
and no way to communicate,
Trump has basically gone silent,

00:03:25.404 --> 00:03:28.541
even as his name is officially
disgraced in history forever.

00:03:28.541 --> 00:03:30.876 line:0%
-This day that the President
is likely to be impeached

00:03:30.876 --> 00:03:33.178 line:0%
in a historic manner
for the second time,

00:03:33.178 --> 00:03:35.147 line:0%
the only president
to ever be impeached twice,

00:03:35.147 --> 00:03:37.116 line:0%
and he has no legal strategy
right now,

00:03:37.116 --> 00:03:40.186 line:0%
and he doesn't even really have
a legal team put together.

00:03:40.186 --> 00:03:42.822 line:0%
There is no
comprehensive strategy
happening behind the scenes.

00:03:42.822 --> 00:03:45.758 line:0%
The President
is basically invisible today.

00:03:47.994 --> 00:03:52.031
-I'm sorry, I was just enjoying
the words "Trump is invisible."

00:03:52.031 --> 00:03:54.666
Do you know how hard it is for a
guy like Trump to go invisible?

00:03:54.666 --> 00:03:56.368
He's not exactly stealth.

00:03:56.368 --> 00:03:59.004
He's invisible the way my kids
are during hide-and-seek.

00:03:59.004 --> 00:04:00.706
Hmm, either they've
left the country,

00:04:00.706 --> 00:04:03.142
or that giggling curtain
is a clue.

00:04:03.142 --> 00:04:04.644
And, honestly, however you feel

00:04:04.644 --> 00:04:06.345
about the merits
of the Twitter ban,

00:04:06.345 --> 00:04:08.614
it's a huge
quality-of-life improvement.

00:04:08.614 --> 00:04:10.149
It's like waking up
the morning after

00:04:10.149 --> 00:04:12.285
construction finally stops
outside your window.

00:04:12.285 --> 00:04:15.221
We no longer have to put up
with President Jackhammer.

00:04:15.221 --> 00:04:17.856
In fact, the last time
we saw Trump was yesterday

00:04:17.856 --> 00:04:21.060
when he flew to Texas
to defend his seditious speech

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:22.427
that whipped up
the violent mob

00:04:22.427 --> 00:04:25.297
and celebrate the entirely
useless monument to racism

00:04:25.297 --> 00:04:26.632
he forced us to pay for,

00:04:26.632 --> 00:04:28.700
despite scamming his supporters
into thinking

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:30.469
it would be paid for by Mexico.

00:04:30.469 --> 00:04:33.506
And if it's the last time
we ever see him on camera
as president,

00:04:33.506 --> 00:04:35.541
I think it'll be fitting
because it ended

00:04:35.541 --> 00:04:37.110
in the most pathetic way
imaginable,

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:40.213
with him quietly slinking
off the stage by himself

00:04:40.213 --> 00:04:43.015
as "YMCA" blasted
over the speakers.

00:04:43.015 --> 00:04:46.986
♪♪

00:04:46.986 --> 00:04:50.189
I hope that's remembered
alongside Nixon on the chopper

00:04:50.189 --> 00:04:51.857
as the last time
we saw him as president

00:04:51.857 --> 00:04:53.293
because it is the opposite

00:04:53.293 --> 00:04:54.760
of the strength
he tries to project,

00:04:54.760 --> 00:04:57.496
just moping away
during a Village People song

00:04:57.496 --> 00:04:59.298
like he just got kicked out
of a wedding

00:04:59.298 --> 00:05:00.700
for trying to hit on the bride.

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:02.401
"How was I supposed to know?

00:05:02.401 --> 00:05:05.605
Oh, right,
the white dress and the veil?

00:05:05.605 --> 00:05:08.074
Oh, yeah, and the groom
did give her that ring.

00:05:08.074 --> 00:05:10.143
Oh, and the vows."

00:05:10.143 --> 00:05:13.546
And it is a testament, a true
testament to the Village People,

00:05:13.546 --> 00:05:16.014
by the way, that even after
that pathetic scene,

00:05:16.014 --> 00:05:17.783
that song still slaps.

00:05:17.783 --> 00:05:19.952
When they eventually arrest
Trump for sedition or incitement

00:05:19.952 --> 00:05:22.455
or tax fraud or extortion
or campaign finance violation

00:05:22.455 --> 00:05:25.524
or, I don't know, any of the 87
crimes he's probably committed,

00:05:25.524 --> 00:05:27.859
I hope they play "YMCA"
during that perp walk.

00:05:27.859 --> 00:05:29.428
I mean, he already dances

00:05:29.428 --> 00:05:32.031
like he's trying to wriggle
out of a pair of handcuffs.

00:05:32.031 --> 00:05:35.301
I also really hope that wasn't
the song that was
supposed to play.

00:05:35.301 --> 00:05:38.504
I really hope it was
a small act of resistance

00:05:38.504 --> 00:05:40.472
by whoever was running
the soundboard,

00:05:40.472 --> 00:05:42.942
that they were supposed to play
"Hail to the Chief"
or something.

00:05:42.942 --> 00:05:45.444
But as they watched
this sack of depravity

00:05:45.444 --> 00:05:47.246
wrap up yet another
lie-filled speech,

00:05:47.246 --> 00:05:49.348
they thought, "[Bleep] it.

00:05:49.348 --> 00:05:51.150
I'm playing 'YMCA.'"

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:55.254
-♪ It's fun to stay
at the YMCA ♪

00:05:55.254 --> 00:05:56.889
-So whatever else happens
after today,

00:05:56.889 --> 00:05:58.924
it'll be inscribed
in the Congressional record

00:05:58.924 --> 00:06:00.259
and in the history books,

00:06:00.259 --> 00:06:01.761
and it'll be a stain
on Trump's name forever.

00:06:01.761 --> 00:06:04.964
He's the only president
to get impeached twice.

00:06:04.964 --> 00:06:06.198
In fact, it's worse than that.

00:06:06.198 --> 00:06:08.234
He's the only president
to be impeached twice

00:06:08.234 --> 00:06:10.669
and lose the popular vote twice.

00:06:10.669 --> 00:06:12.338
He'll be emblazoned in history

00:06:12.338 --> 00:06:13.739
as an embarrassment
and disgrace.

00:06:13.739 --> 00:06:15.541
No politician
has ever been more thoroughly

00:06:15.541 --> 00:06:17.843
and more frequently repudiated
by the American people.

00:06:17.843 --> 00:06:19.812
It's like entering
the Tour de France,

00:06:19.812 --> 00:06:22.348
coming in dead last, and getting
kicked out for steroids,

00:06:22.348 --> 00:06:23.749
then entering again
the next year,

00:06:23.749 --> 00:06:25.151
only to forget your bike,

00:06:25.151 --> 00:06:27.019
forcing you to steal
someone else's, and scream,

00:06:27.019 --> 00:06:31.124
"You'll never catch me,"
before crashing into a cow...

00:06:32.525 --> 00:06:34.327
In 2016,
he lost the popular vote,

00:06:34.327 --> 00:06:36.796
in 2018, he lost the House,
2020 was impeached,

00:06:36.796 --> 00:06:38.564
lost the popular vote
and the Electoral College.

00:06:38.564 --> 00:06:41.467
In 2021, he lost the Senate,
and then he was impeached again.

00:06:41.467 --> 00:06:43.635
It's almost like
he's tanking the season

00:06:43.635 --> 00:06:46.605
so he can get the number-one
pick in the jailhouse
fantasy draft.

00:06:46.605 --> 00:06:49.708
"I'll take Madoff. Hey, Bernie,
I got some real tax issues."

00:06:49.708 --> 00:06:52.578
If nothing else happens
after this, at the bare minimum,

00:06:52.578 --> 00:06:54.980
Trump will be an answer
to a Trivial Pursuit question.

00:06:54.980 --> 00:06:56.682
They'll have to devote
the entire card,

00:06:56.682 --> 00:06:58.717
that little section at the end
where they give you

00:06:58.717 --> 00:07:00.619
an extra tidbit of information.

00:07:00.619 --> 00:07:03.889
"Who's the only president
to be impeached twice?"

00:07:03.889 --> 00:07:06.325
"Huh? Donald Trump.
And it says here,

00:07:06.325 --> 00:07:08.394
'He was impeached for trying
to extort a foreign country

00:07:08.394 --> 00:07:09.962
to help him cheat
in the 2020 election

00:07:09.962 --> 00:07:11.564
and then for inciting
a violent insurrection

00:07:11.564 --> 00:07:12.865
after losing that election.

00:07:12.865 --> 00:07:14.467
And also, he told people
to inject bleach

00:07:14.467 --> 00:07:16.068
during a deadly pandemic
he failed to stop,

00:07:16.068 --> 00:07:18.036
tried to ban Muslims,
called Mexicans rapists,

00:07:18.036 --> 00:07:20.239
paid hush money to cover up
an affair with a porn star,

00:07:20.239 --> 00:07:21.941
and his lawyer
held a press conference

00:07:21.941 --> 00:07:24.943
at a landscaping company,
and see attached brochure
for more.'"

00:07:24.943 --> 00:07:26.278
Wow.

00:07:26.278 --> 00:07:29.148
But as notable as it is
that a few prominent Republicans

00:07:29.148 --> 00:07:30.182
broke with Trump today,

00:07:30.182 --> 00:07:31.750
the fact remains
that the vast majority

00:07:31.750 --> 00:07:33.019
of the House Republican caucus

00:07:33.019 --> 00:07:35.220
sided with him even after
he incited an insurrection

00:07:35.220 --> 00:07:36.889
against the government
a week ago.

00:07:36.889 --> 00:07:38.524
A majority of that same caucus
voted

00:07:38.524 --> 00:07:41.394
to overturn the results of
the election at Trump's behest,

00:07:41.394 --> 00:07:43.629
even after the violent mob
ransacked the Capitol.

00:07:43.629 --> 00:07:45.631 line:0%
And now Republicans
have the gall

00:07:45.631 --> 00:07:48.067 line:0%
to blame Democrats
for sowing disunity.

00:07:48.067 --> 00:07:51.170 line:0%
-What I'm trying to suggest
to you is that both sides
are at fault.

00:07:51.170 --> 00:07:53.806 line:0%
-This is a reckless impeachment.

00:07:53.806 --> 00:07:59.879 line:0%
This will only bring up the hate
and fire more than ever before.

00:07:59.879 --> 00:08:02.081 line:0%
-In seven days, there will be
a peaceful transfer of power,

00:08:02.081 --> 00:08:06.018 line:0%
just like there has been
every other time in our country.

00:08:06.018 --> 00:08:10.489 line:0%
But Democrats are going to
impeach President Trump again.

00:08:10.489 --> 00:08:12.791 line:0%
This doesn't unite the country.

00:08:12.791 --> 00:08:14.226 line:0%
-You don't merely seek victory,

00:08:14.226 --> 00:08:16.762 line:0%
but you seek obliteration
of your nemesis.

00:08:16.762 --> 00:08:19.698 line:0%
-Every movement
has a lunatic fringe.

00:08:19.698 --> 00:08:21.200
-That's your defense?

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:23.435
Look, every movement
has armed militias

00:08:23.435 --> 00:08:25.204
with tactical gear
and zip ties

00:08:25.204 --> 00:08:26.906
and detailed plans
to seize the Capitol

00:08:26.906 --> 00:08:30.275
and Confederate sympathizers
and a Q-Anon antler man.

00:08:30.275 --> 00:08:31.744
You guys are talking about this

00:08:31.744 --> 00:08:34.913
like your [bleep] teenage son
TP'd the principal's house.

00:08:34.913 --> 00:08:38.117
"Look, we've all been there.
You're young and impressionable.

00:08:38.117 --> 00:08:39.652
You downed a few Natty Lights,

00:08:39.652 --> 00:08:41.086
and you tried
to overthrow democracy.

00:08:41.086 --> 00:08:43.556
It happens. Look,
he's graduating in seven days."

00:08:43.556 --> 00:08:45.057
Also, stop saying
Trump is committed

00:08:45.057 --> 00:08:46.525
to a peaceful transfer of power.

00:08:46.525 --> 00:08:48.193
That ship has sailed or, rather,

00:08:48.193 --> 00:08:50.963
that ship was boarded by pirates
and steered into the rocks.

00:08:50.963 --> 00:08:53.031
You guys tried
to overturn an election.

00:08:53.031 --> 00:08:54.700
You sowed an insurrection.

00:08:54.700 --> 00:08:57.669
And now the Capitol has to be
protected by the National Guard

00:08:57.669 --> 00:08:59.672
because there are credible
threats of violence

00:08:59.672 --> 00:09:02.074
from the President's supporters.
That's not peaceful.

00:09:02.074 --> 00:09:04.977
You don't get to throw a brick
through your neighbor's window

00:09:04.977 --> 00:09:06.912
with a note saying,
"Trim your hedges,"

00:09:06.912 --> 00:09:09.281
then when you get caught say,
"Okay, okay, fine.

00:09:09.281 --> 00:09:11.683
Let's just barbecue this out
and put it all behind us.

00:09:11.683 --> 00:09:13.852
Yes, I broke your window,
and, yes,

00:09:13.852 --> 00:09:17.790
I terrified your family,
but you got a free brick."

00:09:17.790 --> 00:09:19.992 line:0%
Also, it's truly disgusting
to suggest

00:09:19.992 --> 00:09:22.361 line:0%
that holding someone accountable
for stoking violence

00:09:22.361 --> 00:09:24.629 line:0%
will itself stoke more violence.

00:09:24.629 --> 00:09:25.897 line:0%
Try that strategy
in a courtroom.

00:09:25.897 --> 00:09:27.833
"Look, if we anger OJ
by convicting him,

00:09:27.833 --> 00:09:29.301
he's just going to
murder again."

00:09:29.301 --> 00:09:31.437
But just to give you
even more of an idea

00:09:31.437 --> 00:09:32.771
of how crazy these people are,

00:09:32.771 --> 00:09:34.339
here's Ohio Congressman
Jim Jordan

00:09:34.339 --> 00:09:35.875
and Colorado Congressman
Ken Buck

00:09:35.875 --> 00:09:37.576 line:0%
rambling through
their usual spiel

00:09:37.576 --> 00:09:39.545 line:0%
of empty slogans
and right-wing buzzwords

00:09:39.545 --> 00:09:41.680 line:0%
about, honestly, God knows what.

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:43.415 line:0%
-They want to cancel
the President.

00:09:43.415 --> 00:09:45.918 line:0%
They spied on his campaign
before he was elected.

00:09:45.918 --> 00:09:47.653 line:0%
Nineteen minutes
into his presidency,

00:09:47.653 --> 00:09:49.421 line:0%
they started
the impeachment push.

00:09:49.421 --> 00:09:50.956 line:0%
Three-year
Mueller investigation --

00:09:50.956 --> 00:09:56.195 line:0%
19 lawyers, 40 agents,
500 witnesses, 2,500 subpoenas,

00:09:56.195 --> 00:09:59.098 line:0%
$40 million to find nothing.

00:09:59.098 --> 00:10:02.768 line:0%
Impeachment round one, based on
an anonymous whistleblower

00:10:02.768 --> 00:10:05.270 line:0%
with no firsthand knowledge,
who was biased against
the President,

00:10:05.270 --> 00:10:07.005 line:0%
and who worked for Joe Biden.

00:10:07.005 --> 00:10:08.374 line:0%
It's not just about
impeachment anymore.

00:10:08.374 --> 00:10:09.775 line:0%
It's about canceling,
as I've said --

00:10:09.775 --> 00:10:13.545 line:0%
canceling the President and
anyone that disagrees with them.

00:10:13.545 --> 00:10:16.181 line:0%
The ayatollah can tweet,
the President can't.

00:10:16.181 --> 00:10:19.218 line:0%
-This House spoke over and over
about impeaching the President

00:10:19.218 --> 00:10:21.687 line:0%
days into his administration.

00:10:21.687 --> 00:10:23.856 line:0%
And then the socialists
in Hollywood

00:10:23.856 --> 00:10:26.058 line:0%
joined their allies in Congress.

00:10:26.058 --> 00:10:29.294 line:0%
Robert De Niro said

00:10:29.294 --> 00:10:31.597 line:0%
that he wanted to punch
the President in the face.

00:10:31.597 --> 00:10:34.066 line:0%
Madonna thought about
blowing up the White House.

00:10:34.066 --> 00:10:36.769 line:0%
Kathy Griffin held up a likeness

00:10:36.769 --> 00:10:39.572 line:0%
of the President's
beheaded head.

00:10:39.572 --> 00:10:42.274 line:0%
And nothing was said
by my colleagues

00:10:42.274 --> 00:10:43.508 line:0%
at that point in time.

00:10:43.508 --> 00:10:45.076
-The President is being
impeached for inciting

00:10:45.076 --> 00:10:47.479
a violent insurrection,
and you're talking about Madonna

00:10:47.479 --> 00:10:49.114
and the ayatollah's
Twitter account?

00:10:49.114 --> 00:10:50.149
What the [bleep]
is wrong with you?

00:10:50.149 --> 00:10:51.417
Is Jim Jordan a real person

00:10:51.417 --> 00:10:53.452
or just a haunted doll
with a string on his back?

00:10:53.452 --> 00:10:56.454
Listening to these guys is like
far-right slam poetry.

00:10:56.454 --> 00:10:59.624
Mueller spy, Madonna lie,

00:10:59.624 --> 00:11:01.761
the ayatollah's
a Twitter guy.

00:11:01.761 --> 00:11:03.863
Although, I have to say,
the take for me

00:11:03.863 --> 00:11:05.230
that is mind-blowingly dumb

00:11:05.230 --> 00:11:07.132
is the argument
that impeaching a president

00:11:07.132 --> 00:11:09.768
for inciting an insurrection
to overthrow democracy

00:11:09.768 --> 00:11:11.270
is cancel culture.

00:11:11.270 --> 00:11:12.904
"They're trying to cancel
the President.

00:11:12.904 --> 00:11:14.940
One day you can't go to Costco
without a mask,

00:11:14.940 --> 00:11:17.009
the next day, you can't try
to overthrow the government.

00:11:17.009 --> 00:11:18.877
What's next?
Soon they're going to say

00:11:18.877 --> 00:11:20.812
you can't go to Supercuts
with a garbage bag

00:11:20.812 --> 00:11:22.548
and ask to collect
the loose hair on the ground

00:11:22.548 --> 00:11:24.683
so you can paste it to your head
like I do.

00:11:24.683 --> 00:11:26.852
When will cancel culture end?"

00:11:26.852 --> 00:11:28.420
These people are deranged.

00:11:28.420 --> 00:11:30.422
They never fail to make
themselves the victims.

00:11:30.422 --> 00:11:31.656
And they think
they're above the rules.

00:11:31.656 --> 00:11:33.392
They think
they're above democracy.

00:11:33.392 --> 00:11:34.794
It's why they think
they should be allowed

00:11:34.794 --> 00:11:36.195
to substitute their own judgment

00:11:36.195 --> 00:11:37.696
for the will
of 81 million Americans

00:11:37.696 --> 00:11:39.031
who voted for Joe Biden.

00:11:39.031 --> 00:11:40.565
It's why when you
politely ask them

00:11:40.565 --> 00:11:41.933
to walk through metal detectors

00:11:41.933 --> 00:11:43.435
a week after the Capitol
was seized

00:11:43.435 --> 00:11:44.503
by right-wing terrorists,

00:11:44.503 --> 00:11:46.371
they ignore them
and whine about them

00:11:46.371 --> 00:11:48.040
and lose their minds
like Nicolas Cage

00:11:48.040 --> 00:11:49.141
in "The Wicker Man."

00:11:49.141 --> 00:11:52.477
-[ Screaming ]

00:11:52.477 --> 00:11:55.614
-The President and his allies
in the GOP and right-wing media

00:11:55.614 --> 00:11:57.882
have spent years
feeding their rabid fan base

00:11:57.882 --> 00:12:00.619
deranged lies and fantasies
of violent retribution,

00:12:00.619 --> 00:12:03.355
culminating with the effort
to overturn the election

00:12:03.355 --> 00:12:04.623
in a violent insurrection.

00:12:04.623 --> 00:12:06.658
Trump watched it,
gleefully encouraged it,

00:12:06.658 --> 00:12:08.227
and even when
members of Congress

00:12:08.227 --> 00:12:09.928
pleaded with him to stop it,
refused.

00:12:09.928 --> 00:12:12.464
And in the end,
just 10 Republicans
voted to impeach him.

00:12:12.464 --> 00:12:15.200
If you're asking whether
it should have been more...

00:12:15.200 --> 00:12:16.368
-The answer is yes.

00:12:16.368 --> 00:12:18.871
This has been "A Closer Look."

